 Text, transcription, speech, and image inference are implemented and verified on Mac staging and Linux CPU. Production deployment on `squarebrothers_vps`, representative model-quality evaluation, and user acceptance remain pending. A management UI is future work. Trusted SSH host-key confirmation and remote hardware inspection precede production deployment. Follow [GOAL.md](GOAL.md) and [docs/architecture.md](docs/architecture.md) for the remaining work.
+
+## Optional inference-only credential
+
+Set `MODEL_HOST_INFERENCE_TOKEN` in the environment's private configuration to a
+separate strong random value. It can list models and call the `/v1` text, audio
+and image inference routes; it cannot use `/api` management routes. The existing
+`MODEL_HOST_TOKEN` remains the management credential and is required when the
+inference credential is set. The credentials must differ. If the inference
+credential is absent, existing authentication behavior is unchanged. These
+credentials do not replace TLS for access over an untrusted network.
+
+The scoped-token lifecycle fixtures run with `MODEL_HOST_TEST_BIN` pointing to a
+locally built host. The cross-project checks additionally require
+`ARUVI_STUDIO_TEST_BIN` (native) or `ARUVI_STUDIO_TEST_IMAGE` and
+`ARUVI_STUDIO_ROOT` (Docker). They create disposable state and use simulated
+workers and synthetic credentials; they do not validate real-model quality.
+The optional `tests/studio_scoped_rotation.py` fixture uses the same Docker
+variables and checks that Studio's watcher handles a scoped-token change before
+and after an isolated host restart without replacing the provider.
